  "notes": "{騙|だま}す implies intentional deception to gain advantage or cause harm.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Takes ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ particle: ⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{騙|だま}す\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦{人|ひと}→人：00476_hito⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{騙|だま}す: to deceive someone\n- {騙|だま}されないで: don't be fooled\n- ⟦うまく→うまい：01279_umai⟧{騙|だま}す: to trick cleverly\n- ⟦{金|かね}→金：02618_kane⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{騙|だま}し⟦{取|と}る→取る：00565_toru⟧: to swindle money\n\nPASSIVE FORM:\n{騙|だま}される is very common, meaning \"to be deceived\" or \"to fall for a trick.\"\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{詐欺|さぎ}→詐欺：09789_sagi⟧: fraud, scam\n- ⟦{嘘|うそ}→嘘：01796_uso⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦つく→つく：noentry⟧: to tell a lie (less malicious)\n- ⟦{欺|あざむ}く→欺く：13171_azamuku⟧: to deceive (literary)",
